{"title":"2005 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle having center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/6/c0658fa5f64bbe8fbe318420d63186079e262dc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/c/37c964b299574421c69f6a7db7e80f43b23e2887.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;6$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, is tangent to the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741a74d86df899c10724dc2f80638f5e7f599194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/0/7f08809818fd50ee3fc13182a3112bc2bd28dccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daaf07d9f0a2413768e291d1264b59b3c835e4aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />. What is the radius of this circle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/3/3c32bcd16ebe7fcacb23d4ddc49ab0aede4ffffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 6\\sqrt{2}-6 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C)}\\ 6\\sqrt{2} \\qquad \\mathrm{(D)}\\ 12 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E)}\\ 6+6\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"487\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the radius of the circle. Draw the two radii that meet the points of tangency to the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/6581b84e5cb5d62342b862c8a165b47803c1f3a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\pm x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />. We can see that a square is formed by the origin, two tangency points, and the center of the circle. The side lengths of this square are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and the diagonal is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/5/5252fd427f17ab2cbe9143e26b1ce401970d6f9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = R+6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" />. The diagonal of a square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4dc1409208ff6a3039f4871d85c16763334983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" /> times the side length. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/023b53e75fc041f7731ad58a56f30b209e1c309b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R+6 = R\\sqrt{2} \\Rightarrow R = \\dfrac{6}{\\sqrt{2}-1} = 6+6\\sqrt{2} \\Rightarrow \\boxed{\\mathrm{E}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"375\" height=\"42\" />. \n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/1/9214d60dfddf137d3b4e216cf2abcdd4d76c8e90.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] real Xmin,Xmax,Ymin,Ymax; real R = 6+6*sqrt(2); Xmin = -16; Xmax = 16; Ymin = -4; Ymax = 40; xaxis(Xmin,Xmax,Arrows); yaxis(Ymin,Ymax,Arrows);  label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(Xmax+0.25,0),S); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,(0,Ymax+0.25),E); draw((Xmin,-Xmin)--(-Ymin,Ymin)); draw((Xmax,Xmax)--(Ymin,Ymin)); draw((Xmin,6)--(Xmax,6)); dot((0,0)); dot((R/sqrt(2),R/sqrt(2))); dot((-R/sqrt(2),R/sqrt(2))); dot((0,R*sqrt(2))); draw((0,0)--(R/sqrt(2),R/sqrt(2))--(0,R*sqrt(2))--(-R/sqrt(2),R/sqrt(2))--(0,0)); draw(Circle((0,6+R),R)); label(&quot;$R$&quot;,(0,6+R/2),(0,0));  label(&quot;$R$&quot;,(-R/(2*sqrt(2)),3*R/(2*sqrt(2))),0.5*NW);  label(&quot;$R$&quot;,(R/(2*sqrt(2)),3*R/(2*sqrt(2))),0.5*NE); label(&quot;$R$&quot;,(-R/(2*sqrt(2)),R/(2*sqrt(2))),0.5*SW);  label(&quot;$R$&quot;,(R/(2*sqrt(2)),R/(2*sqrt(2))),0.5*SE); label(&quot;$6$&quot;,(0,3),(0,0)); [/asy]\" width=\"185\" height=\"252\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B\" title=\"2005 AMC 12B\">2005 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td